rradius installed from the port
===============================

The port installs the program, the RADIUS dictionaries and the documentation, and creates the
user "rradius" and the directories /var/db/rradius (data) and /var/log/rradius. It does not
create a configuration and does not start the service.

First start
-----------

  1. Print a starting configuration; it has random cluster and client secrets:

       rradius-server config init > /usr/local/etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  2. Point "dictionary" at /usr/local/share/rradius/dictionary, set the cluster data
     directory (for example /var/db/rradius), add the [lua] script and your clients, and keep the
     file readable by the "rradius" user only:

       chown root:rradius /usr/local/etc/rradius/rradius.toml && chmod 640 /usr/local/etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  3. Check, enable and start:

       rradius-server check
       sysrc rradius_enable=YES
       service rradius start

The default configuration path is fixed when the program is built; "rradius-server --version"
shows it on the second line.

The program runs as the "rradius" user, which cannot bind ports below 1024: TACACS+ on its
standard port 49 needs mac_portacl(4), or the sysctl net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh=0, or a
port of 1024 or above.

The accounting log can be rotated by newsyslog: see
/usr/local/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/rradius.conf.sample.

Documentation: /usr/local/share/doc/rradius/manual/README.md (start there) and usage.md.
